  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PAfID-GEDSI in WRG &amp; Climate Resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">People&#x2019;s Actions for Inclusive Development (PAfID), a non-governmental organization dedicated to fostering inclusive development, particularly for marginalized groups and individuals with disabilities. PAfID works to build the capacity of organizations, governments, and communities, ensuring that people with disabilities have equitable access to social, cultural, and economic opportunities. Its initiatives focus on inclusive governance, employment, rural livelihoods, and leadership empowerment for women with disabilities,promoting meaningful participation and social integration.

Oxfam in Cambodia partners with PAfID to implement IP3 project by building capacity of IP3 partners to develop and implement GEDSI policies or action plans, fostering engagement of people with disabilities and other marginalized groups to participate and influence water governance and climate resilience, identifying the needs of PWDsand ensure their voice and priorities are mainstreamed in the IP3 program/project implementation as well incorporated in sub-national planning and relevant national policies and plans.

Key priorities of PAfID are 1) build capacity of IP3 partners on rights and legal frameworks on PWDs, 2) identify the data and assess the needs of PWDs and other marginalized groups to inform the IP3 partners on the ground to include them in water governance and climate resilience decision making that benefit them, 3) participate and engage PWDs and marginalized groups in water and climate related events or campaigns; and 4) host national dialogues to influence relevant policies to be more inclusive to PWDs and other marginalized groups.</narrative>
  </description>
